# Realtime Tonal-Center Probability (Continuous Chroma)

This repository hosts a staged implementation of a realtime tonal-center probability estimator over a continuous chroma cycle anchored at 220 Hz. The work proceeds in five milestones that mirror the collaboration workflow with Codex:

1. Project scaffolding (current)
2. Continuous Chroma Feature (CCF) extraction and validation with synthetic tones
3. Single-Key Evaluator (SKE) baseline using the Krumhansl–Kessler major profile
4. Tonal-center probability distribution across circular transpositions
5. Realtime visualization pipeline for polar and cylinder views

The source tree is organised to reflect the realtime pipeline: audio ingestion, optional pre-filtering, feature extraction, transposition scanning, key evaluation, and user interface. Every module currently contains structural stubs, type contracts, and documentation TODOs to support incremental development without committing to algorithms prematurely.

## Repository Layout

```
src/ccf_key_detector/
  audio_io/        # Live/file input abstraction and resampling hooks
  prefilter/       # Deterministic voice-friendly filters (gate/HPF)
  features_ccf/    # Spectrum-to-continuous-chroma conversion utilities
  transpose/       # Circular shift operator T and helpers
  ske/             # Single-key evaluator strategies (KK major baseline first)
  rt_viz/          # Realtime visualization modes and buffers
  app/             # Top-level runner and orchestration logic
config/            # Runtime configuration schemas and defaults
tests/             # Placeholder tests for upcoming milestones
```

## Development Notes

- Python 3.10+ is required.
- External dependencies (audio I/O, plotting, GPU) are not yet pinned; they will be added alongside their respective milestone implementations.
- Live input relies on the `sounddevice` package (PortAudio); install system-level audio drivers accordingly if you plan to run the realtime pipeline.
- The 3D surface visualiser requires `pyqtgraph`, `PyQt5`, and `PyOpenGL`; install these before running with `--viz-mode surface`.
- The realtime runner surfaces the KK-major cosine similarity (`ske_score`) for each hop alongside the CCF visualization.
- No file exports (CSV/JSON) are generated during this milestone; realtime-only behaviour is enforced later.

## Test Utilities

- `scripts/generate_mixed_tones.py` synthesises a three-tone clip (250/300/440 Hz) and plots its continuous chroma PDF for quick manual inspection: `PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/generate_mixed_tones.py`.
- `scripts/generate_kk_profile_audio.py` produces a KK-major-profile-matched waveform and prints the resulting SKE score: `PYTHONPATH=src python scripts/generate_kk_profile_audio.py`.
- `scripts/plot_ske_distribution.py <audio.wav>` renders the CCF, KK profile overlay, and full SKE tonal distribution for a given audio file.

Proceed to each milestone by filling the TODO blocks inside the relevant modules. Tests should be upgraded from scaffolding skips to real coverage as functionality lands.
